{"title":"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec7f5c8a2e333c93cce2a88e21f33042eafde614.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0,b_0,c_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> be complex numbers, and define\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca4a66b31e3c693419b2771c78287d9c589fa2f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{n+1}=a_n^2+2b_nc_n\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463e0666030d03bba947553e814096c91db2b329.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b_{n+1}=b_n^2+2c_na_n\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5eceeed057fdd37716fb322b3962ee36433d75ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_{n+1}=c_n^2+2a_nb_n\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\nfor all nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/83560f9ad39323aa08aa51fd2f8c0e369f58d8aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max{|a_n|,|b_n|,|c_n|}\\leq2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad6f3579e7bc550cc761eaa40aa09481da67745.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a_0|^2+|b_0|^2+|c_0|^2\\leq 1.\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8025f6148df44e4d2243629e6f5d47ca7ebe57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n = a_n + b_n + c_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />. Summing the three given recurrences yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b287fdfee262fb46dfbdc7a61d02f4b0495ba1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_{n+1} = a_n^2 + b_n^2 + c_n^2 + 2a_nb_n + 2b_nc_n + 2c_na_n = (a_n + b_n + c_n)^2 = S_n^2\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>By induction, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d93aea7ec7ef5ee83d0bcfa6e2b065b291aa80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n = S_0^{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"22\" />. We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c1a5995588c01de4a72de623b5203af11362e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max(|a_n|, |b_n|, |c_n|) \\le 2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. By the triangle inequality, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e23f7935c7934d37a943c045b490f762e9494a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|S_n| \\le |a_n| + |b_n| + |c_n| \\le 3 \\times 2022 = 6066.\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"18\" />\nSince the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0fe1057d824b741c4c2ce0da4f40428791c2f1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_n|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" /> is bounded, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b9fd7436324d1961966cde20165a303db02733f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_0| \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />. (If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/b/f5bd4aec7e0f309972819888d5c43760d1717709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_0| &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f1e23f6859e34529c15e814471443ccff490c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_n| \\to \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/63405adfa323cd12386536930115984575a36cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\to \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"10\" />, which contradicts the boundedness condition).\n</p><p>Next, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2ffb946e7ddf9068c1003b96b420b0b0837a3a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega = e^{2\\pi i / 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> be a primitive cube root of unity, satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/0371b9415e0fe39090ecae908d594dd0a22ed323.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^3 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc71b6edecc4c9cab3c20c312b63dcc0852d3792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + \\omega + \\omega^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />. We define two new sequences:\n\\begin{align*}\nT_n &amp;= a_n + \\omega b_n + \\omega^2 c_n \\\\\nU_n &amp;= a_n + \\omega^2 b_n + \\omega c_n\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Squaring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fbf1a46d9e0cedde66ffbe8317d0cc7f06e04fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, we obtain:\n\\begin{align*}\nU_n^2 &amp;= (a_n + \\omega^2 b_n + \\omega c_n)^2 \\\\\n&amp;= a_n^2 + \\omega^4 b_n^2 + \\omega^2 c_n^2 + 2\\omega^2 a_nb_n + 2\\omega a_nc_n + 2\\omega^3 b_nc_n \n\\end{align*}\nUsing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/0371b9415e0fe39090ecae908d594dd0a22ed323.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^3 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b69826ab85aa49f0eb08dc1ce14a477a57f5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^4 = \\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />, this simplifies to:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea38a91a7121d61322930583dcb43c17580fbd4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[U_n^2 = a_n^2 + \\omega b_n^2 + \\omega^2 c_n^2 + 2\\omega^2 a_nb_n + 2\\omega a_nc_n + 2b_nc_n\\]\" width=\"402\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Now, let's evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1ef39be9a742204eb7347c5d32c9941e98c69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> using the given recurrences:\n\\begin{align*}\nT_{n+1} &amp;= a_{n+1} + \\omega b_{n+1} + \\omega^2 c_{n+1} \\\\\n&amp;= (a_n^2 + 2b_nc_n) + \\omega(b_n^2 + 2c_na_n) + \\omega^2(c_n^2 + 2a_nb_n)\n\\end{align*}\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1ef39be9a742204eb7347c5d32c9941e98c69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> matches the expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/468ab275fa17c0576e441fbe92e17923a6fdc620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"21\" /> perfectly. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f95e83e18ca1d94127463d3f5595dc6e99a54e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+1} = U_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"21\" />. By a symmetric calculation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f591c0355b68e62879b2c56d4724fabc155d7029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_{n+1} = T_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Combining these two relations, we find that for the even terms:\n\\begin{align*}\nT_{n+2} &amp;= U_{n+1}^2 = (T_n^2)^2 = T_n^4 \\\\\nU_{n+2} &amp;= T_{n+1}^2 = (U_n^2)^2 = U_n^4\n\\end{align*}\nThis implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a677c2068b7eab20b8884262cb3fdf21edc4114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{2k} = T_0^{4^k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"25\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e0bf09f77ca375a3f9d743236e6968999f3c37f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_{2k} = U_0^{4^k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" />. Using the same boundedness argument as before, since the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/4001607b97ff4cb258a743bd78b09d1a7119e4e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n, b_n, c_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> are bounded and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b085f44e9e778d19f0e92b7c6394213fd054206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\omega| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />, the sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e5b35635b75895cb5b4cd3cebfce3157083a038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T_n|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffb9a8f281ae73162ee937ae970d2571a98a36e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|U_n|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"33\" height=\"20\" /> are also strictly bounded. Therefore, their initial moduli must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/5/d755e0bf52ebec3f7bc66fb050cd920b1bebe162.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|T_0| \\le 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad |U_0| \\le 1\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Finally, we utilize the absolute value squared identity in the complex plane:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b087ba6035af83faee28f6a96fbf460ce488ffb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|S_0|^2 + |T_0|^2 + |U_0|^2 = S_0\\overline{S_0} + T_0\\overline{T_0} + U_0\\overline{U_0}\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"20\" />\nExpanding this sum, the coefficient of any squared term (such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32cc248dae99a09501ea5d85fb485056f308120c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0\\overline{a_0} = |a_0|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585788df1d33882aeb1371884ad082a7724ed395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 + 1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. The coefficient of any cross term (such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/8264e5292545eb4c8e26b76449806d118258e5b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0\\overline{b_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"21\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc71b6edecc4c9cab3c20c312b63dcc0852d3792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + \\omega + \\omega^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />, meaning all cross terms cancel out completely. Thus, we obtain:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/7030f51330abfec125eb45ff04586da51bb1457e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|S_0|^2 + |T_0|^2 + |U_0|^2 = 3(|a_0|^2 + |b_0|^2 + |c_0|^2)\\]\" width=\"342\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b9fd7436324d1961966cde20165a303db02733f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_0| \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c29c7b69622a007d313ac0a16d00afb563fa59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T_0| \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/6289984d4a74e2bf0ffdca22f1b73d40553977c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|U_0| \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />, the maximum possible value of the left-hand side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4f4c34232fd5fd8e98b7fb7be7c8846347a0380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore:\n\\begin{align*}\n3(|a_0|^2 + |b_0|^2 + |c_0|^2) &amp;\\le 3 \\\\\n|a_0|^2 + |b_0|^2 + |c_0|^2 &amp;\\le 1\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>This completes the proof.\n</p><p><br />\n~BennyWang\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO\" title=\"2022 USAJMO\">2022 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2022\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017054106\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 285/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9190/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.477      1 -total\n 70.60%   12.338      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 28.20%    4.929      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22661:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017054106 and revision id 284035. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}